[Music]  this is a visualization of the different  paths the key figures took during the  course of the great calamity it's based  on the information provided to us by  creating a champion  as well as different cut scenes from  breath of the wild over the course of  this demonstration we will pause the  narrative at various moments to analyze  and cross-reference this information  with some of the cutscenes seen in the  trailer of the newly announced hyrule  warriors  age of calamity the goal is to see if  this holds up to the pre-existing  knowledge of the event as well as  provide possible scenarios for the  aforementioned game  so anytime you see this text pop up we  will sketch a possible gameplay scenario  and make best guesses on how this might  turn out this is part 1 of a 7 part  series which will be published up until  the 26th of september when we are  supposedly getting more information  about the sequel to hyrule warriors  when all parts are released there will  be a full version available with all  characters included the one you are  watching right now will focus on lincoln  zelda and i will be joined by none other  than nintendo black crisis in this part  he too will be posting his own video  which focuses on the lore comparisons  between breath of the wild and hyrule  warriors age of calamity as well as  story predictions for the game  so be sure to check that one out too the  link will be in the description  a couple of things to note this series  will only cover the events  during the great calamity itself from  the moment it starts until the moment  zelda seals ganon inside hyrule castle  any moments before or after  are simply too speculative and we don't  have enough information about these  events  this includes any monster attacks that  may have occurred before calamity ganon  rose up from the castle  additionally we will focus solely on the  key players in the story and their  actions during the disaster  it will not feature detailed  descriptions of battles taking place  or the fate of the many towns villages  and garrisons  with that said let's get into it  despite being dubbed the day of the  great calamity the event itself doesn't  actually last throughout the whole day  at sunrise zelda travels to the  promenade with four of the five  champions accompanying her  as according to ravali's diary he  himself arrived much later  from here she scales mount leneru to  pray at the spring of wisdom  with link watching over her at sundown  ravali has finally joined the party  link and zelda return from the summit  and are greeted by the four pilots  after some conversation the earth starts  to tremble and the sky in the distance  starts to glow in eerie red color rivali  flies up to see what's happening  and witnesses the ghostly figure that is  calamity ganon  swirling around above hyrule castle this  officially marks the beginning of the  calamity  and this is where our analysis begins  after briefly discussing their strategy  the party splits up into different  directions  linc and zelda traverse the promenade  through the canyon and towards kakariko  village  after crossing the village they make  their way down sahasrara's slope and  follow hylia river past the linearu  wetlands  they reach rabone bridge and cross into  central hyrule  through may prairie and towards the  gates of hyrule castletown  by the time they arrive hyrule castle is  burning and the town square is about to  be ravaged by guardians  they quickly realize that the castle and  town  are beyond saving creating a champion  does not specify how long link and zelda  lingered on the central square  it's highly likely that age of calamity  will make this a playable section in  which link and zelda desperately try to  fight off as many enemies as possible  this way they grant some of the soldiers  and civilians a chance to escape the  city  it's also likely that they will be  joined by impa in this fight based  on this still frame where they are seen  in front of the gates of castletown with  impa at their side  after realizing the town is lost the duo  is forced to make the difficult decision  of leaving their friends and family to  their fate  and prioritize their own survival at  this point the guardians are about to  spill out into the green fields of  central hyrule through the main gate  as well as the east and west gate of  castletown towards the quarry and  to akala citadel in pursuit of the  fleeing population  link and zelda make their way to mabe  village and its nearby ranch  as its closest neighbors to castle town  these are the first two settlements to  come under siege by the machines  unlike most regular villages across  hyrule mabe village seems to be well  defended as seen from this screenshot  the town has a wall  and a gate and from studying the ruins  of mabe village we can find multiple  dead guardians  something that's exceptionally rare to  see in the other destroyed villages  it's possible that age of calamity will  see link and zelda take part in the  defense of the village for a while  before continuing onwards  after crossing mabe village the two once  again crossed the mabe prairie  however unlike the previous route they  took when they were on the way to the  castle  something interesting happens right as  they are about to cross the rabone  bridge  they make an abrupt turn and head south  along the other side of the hylia river  this sudden change of direction  indicates that the guardians approaching  from the north and northeast  forced them to change course this falls  in line with the attack on gapunga  village which is situated in the lenairu  wetlands  by the time the duo reaches the bridge  the guardians which rushed from the east  gate had likely already reached the  other side of the river  pushing them south in all likelihood  linc and zelda originally planned to  take the same route they did  before up the hash's slope and towards  kakariko village  it's the most logical option for a safe  haven and impa likely urged  zelda to rendezvous at the village with  their intended escape route now blocked  the two moved south  sticking to the riverbank and avoiding  major settlements their goal is to reach  fort hattino the only defensive line on  the way to east nekluda  inside a forest close to the bottomless  swamp zelda briefly breaks down with  link comforting her  but with no time to lose and guardians  on the way she regains her footing and  they continue to move down hilaia river  across horwell bridge and towards the  dueling peaks  from central hyrule an evacuation route  has been set up from the hyrule exchange  all the way to hateno village with  guardians still on their tail lincoln  zelda crossed the squabble river and  joined the evacuation line  age of calamity might turn this pursuit  into an actual gameplay section  where link and zelda may need to stand  their ground and hold back the incoming  guardians in order to keep the  evacuating citizens safe  as the two join the tail end of the  evacuation line they cross between the  dueling peaks  and onto black cherry plain they reach  fort hattano  and this is where the duo makes their  final stand with the help of the fort's  militia they fend off volley after  volley of incoming guardians  each wave takes its toll on our hero  link until finally  he can take no more obviously out of all  memories in breath of the wild link's  final stand  is one of the most iconic moments and  saved for last for a good reason  the defense of fort hattano will most  likely be made playable as either link  or  zelda though in this case link would  definitely be a more fitting choice  after completing this chaotic battle we  will likely transition to the infamous  scene  totally exhausted the hero is about to  make his final sacrifice  and fulfill his duty to protect the  princess one of the guardians detects  his presence and is about to extinguish  his fire once and for all when zelda's  sacred sealing power springs to life  a blast of energy surges across the  fields of blachery plane  and the guardians in its vicinity are no  more  despite this victory for the mortally  wounded link it seems to be too late  he collapses in zelda's arms and just as  all hope seems lost  zelda receives a message from within the  master sword what words were spoken  exactly is unknown as only zelda is able  to hear the message  but it suggests that link can still be  saved if placed in the shrine of  resurrection  with zelda not showing up at kakariko  village according to the plan  the worried impa has dispatched shika  warriors to locate the princess  two of which arrive just in time to aid  her she instructs them to take link back  to the shrine of resurrection  as she feels his survival is key to the  defeat  of calamity gannon from this moment the  paths of the hero and princess diverge  as link is being carried to the shrine  of resurrection along with the sheikah  slate  zelda takes the heavily damaged master  sword and makes her way to kakariko  village to discuss a new strategy  she then sets off on a dangerous journey  alone towards hyrule's great  forest once again she traverses a  sahasrara slope  and moves north this time crossing  them's bridge into tribbly plain  through the minchi woods and into the  forest there  she lay the master sword to rest at the  foot of the great deku tree  after a brief conversation with the  guardian of the forest  she sets off towards hyrule castle past  the military training ground  roru settlement then crosses the  helmhead and boneyard bridge and through  the east gate of castletown  she arrives at her final destination and  stands face to face with the scourge  of hyrule castle calamity ganon  she raises her hand and with a bright  flash of light seals herself  along with the demon kane inside the  castle  zelda's journey is one of if not the  most important moment which took place  during the calamity  there is a high probability that this  section will be playable  although zelda's move set seems to  revolve around the use of the sheikah  slate as seen in the trailer  she will most likely wield her sacred  power in this section of the game  perhaps in the form of the bow of light  or simply by creating energy blasts to  rid her of the enemies standing in her  way  meanwhile as zelda is on our way to  hyrule castle link has arrived at the  great plateau and is placed inside the  shrine of resurrection  additionally impa has instructed pura  and robbie to join them as their  expertise and knowledge of the facility  is needed to operate it  link is laid to rest and the sheikah  slade is placed inside a pedestal  alongside him in hopes that it will be  of use to him when he finally wakes up  the moment zelda sealed ganon inside the  castle the events of the calamity  largely came to a halt  forced into a dormant state he loses  direct control over the guardians and  divine beasts  the beasts shut down and become inactive  as for the guardians  those who are still operational either  retreat back to hyrule castle  or mindlessly wander the landscape  without a clear purpose  [Music]  you

